<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Managing Change for Successful Healthcare CRM Adoption</b></h3>
                <p>
                    CRM adoption depends on how well users understand and integrate new workflows into their daily activities. A structured change strategy helps teams gain value from the platform.
                </p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Explain the CRM Vision: Clearly communicate how the CRM will improve engagement, coordination, visibility, and productivity.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Engage Business Users: Involve healthcare, administrative, marketing, service, and management stakeholders in solution design.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Provide Role-Based Training: Train users on the CRM capabilities and workflows relevant to their roles.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Roll Out in Phases: Introduce CRM capabilities in manageable stages and monitor adoption.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Provide Ongoing Support: Address user questions, review usage, and continuously optimize CRM processes.
                        </p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />
                <h3><b>How to Optimize Healthcare CRM for Maximum ROI</b></h3>
                <p>
                    A healthcare CRM should continuously evolve to support stronger engagement, better productivity, and measurable operational outcomes.
                </p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Define CRM KPIs: Measure engagement, response times, follow-up completion, referral activity, and other relevant outcomes.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Integrate Core Systems: Connect CRM with patient, scheduling, communication, analytics, and other business applications.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Improve User Experience: Simplify screens, workflows, and tasks to improve adoption and productivity.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Review CRM Performance: Regularly assess workflows, data quality, adoption, and business outcomes.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Leverage Automation and Analytics: Use automation, reporting, and intelligent insights to improve engagement and decision-making.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-4 Imgborder">
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/Developer2.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" /></div>
